### Bookings module — manual requests (REST Client extension for VS Code)
#
# How to use:
# 1. Install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) in VS Code.
# 2. Open this file. Above each request block you'll see a small
#    "Send Request" link — click it to fire that specific request.
# 3. Make sure the API is running (npm run dev) before sending requests.
# 4. Edit the values in the JSON bodies freely to try different cases.
# 5. baseUrl comes from the active REST Client environment (bottom-right
#    of VS Code) — see .vscode/settings.json for "local" vs "production".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tokens setup
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin token: there is no endpoint to register as ADMIN directly. Run the
# seed script to create/update an admin user from the ADMIN_SEED_* vars
# in .env:
#   npm run prisma:seed
# Then log in with those credentials via auth/auth.http (POST /auth/login,
# using ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL/ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD from .env) and paste the
# returned accessToken below.
@adminToken = replace-with-admin-token

# Regular user token: register/login normally via auth/auth.http
# (POST /auth/register then POST /auth/login) and paste the token below.
@userToken = replace-with-user-token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other ids you'll need
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# roomId: copy it from rooms.http, either from the "List all rooms" response
# or from the room you created with "Create a room".
@roomId = replace-with-room-id

# bookingId: copy it from the response body of "Create a booking (happy
# path)" below, once you've sent that request.
@bookingId = replace-with-booking-id

# userId: the id of the logged-in user (@userToken), used below as a
# filter for GET /bookings and to test the non-admin 403 case. You can
# get it by decoding the JWT, or from the register/login response body.
@userId = replace-with-user-id

### Create a booking (happy path)
# Requires @userToken and @roomId to be set above.
# Business hours are 8:00–20:00 Argentina time (America/Argentina/Buenos_Aires).
# Using the -03:00 offset directly in the ISO string is simpler than
# converting to UTC by hand.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T10:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T11:00:00-03:00"
}

### Get my bookings (requires auth — any logged-in user, only their own bookings)
# Requires @userToken to be set above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### List every booking, no filters (admin only)
# Requires @adminToken to be set above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### List bookings filtered by userId (admin only)
# Requires @adminToken and @userId to be set above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?userId={{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### List bookings filtered by roomId and date (admin only)
# Requires @adminToken and @roomId to be set above. Filters are
# combinable — mix and match date/roomId/userId as needed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?roomId={{roomId}}&date=2026-09-20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Cancel a booking (happy path — owner cancels their own booking)
# Requires @userToken and @bookingId to be set above (see "Create a booking"
# above to get a fresh bookingId).
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error cases
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Error case: create a booking as an admin
# Booking a room is a regular-user action — admins can't book.
# Requires @adminToken and @roomId to be set above. Expect 403 Forbidden.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T10:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T11:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking without the Authorization header
# No token at all — expect 401 Unauthorized.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T10:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T11:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking for a room that doesn't exist
# Expect 404 Not Found — roomId doesn't match any existing room.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T10:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T11:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking outside business hours (too early, 7am)
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — business hours are 8:00–20:00 Argentina time.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T07:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T08:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking outside business hours (too late, ends at 9pm)
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — business hours are 8:00–20:00 Argentina time.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T20:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T21:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking that crosses midnight
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — a booking must fall within a single day.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T19:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-21T01:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking that overlaps an existing one (first request)
# Send this one first — expect 201 Created (or reuse the happy-path
# booking above if you already sent it with this exact time range).
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T14:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T15:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking that overlaps an existing one (second request)
# Same room, overlapping time range as the request right above —
# send this one right after it. Expect 409 Conflict.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T14:30:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T15:30:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking without a roomId
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — roomId is required (Zod validation).
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T10:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T11:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: create a booking where endTime is before startTime
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity (Zod validation).
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "startTime": "2026-09-20T11:00:00-03:00",
  "endTime": "2026-09-20T10:00:00-03:00"
}

### Error case: list bookings without the Authorization header
# No token at all — expect 401 Unauthorized.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings

### Error case: list bookings with a non-admin token
# Valid token, but the user's role isn't ADMIN — expect 403 Forbidden.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Error case: list bookings with an invalid date format
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — date must be YYYY-MM-DD.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?date=20-09-2026
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Error case: list bookings with a roomId that isn't a valid UUID
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?roomId=not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Error case: cancel someone else's booking without being admin
# @userToken belongs to a different user than the one who owns @bookingId —
# expect 403 Forbidden. (To try this for real, create a second user via
# auth.http, log in as them, and use that token here instead.)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Error case: cancel a booking that doesn't exist
# Expect 404 Not Found.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Error case: cancel the same booking twice
# Send the "Cancel a booking (happy path)" request above first, then send
# this exact same request again right after — expect 409 Conflict, since
# cancelling is not idempotent on purpose (an already-cancelled booking
# can't be cancelled again).
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
